+ * bluetoothd took the v1 event as an encryption change, but the command stayed pending: its security manager kept
+ * incoming L2CAP channels waiting ("deferredEnforcerCB busy ... PMAN_ST_SECMGR_ENFORCE", "cid ... not found",
+ * CONFIG_RSP timeouts), and when the command timed out ("HCI expected event 89 with opcode OI_DHCI_SET_CNCT_
+ * ENCRYPTION_OPCODE timedout") bluetoothd restarted (reason 621), dropping the AirPods right after mediaserverd's
+ * "audio started" and AVDTP_Start. Now, while bluetoothd has v2 enabled, each v1 event is given to it as v2 with a
+ * key size of 16 (0 when off); bluetoothd reads the real size itself (Read_Encryption_Key_Size). Also: while a
+ * connection is up, an LE scan window is cut to a quarter of its interval (bluetoothd's active 30/40 ms scans ran
